{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"U-حسن\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The noun حُسْنًا names conduct with practical social force: it appears in calls for good speech to people (2:83) and goodness toward parents (29:8). As an option to adopt فِيهِمْ opposite تُعَذِّبَ, it suggests broad good treatment of this people. Nearby الْحُسْنَىٰ is a distinct form used for the believer’s reward.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"2:83\",\"ar\":\"وَقُولُوا۟ لِلنَّاسِ حُسْنًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"29:8\",\"ar\":\"وَوَصَّيْنَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ بِوَٰلِدَيْهِ حُسْنًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"إِمَّآ أَن تُعَذِّبَ وَإِمَّآ أَن تَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمْ حُسْنًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:88\",\"ar\":\"فَلَهُۥ جَزَآءً ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ ۖ وَسَنَقُولُ لَهُۥ مِنْ أَمْرِنَا يُسْرًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The overt people قَوْمًا, the domain phrase فِيهِمْ, and the contrast with punishment make the interpersonal usages relevant.\",\"limits\":\"These parallels support a range of good treatment but do not specify whether it means mercy, material aid, fair governance, or a combination. The reward term الْحُسْنَىٰ is a distinct form and does not define حُسْنًا.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"X1\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Other ح س ن forms frame goodness in this surah as ethically assessed: 18:7 presents the best deed as a test, while 18:104 describes people who imagine they do good. The outcome in 18:87–88 distinguishes ظلم from faith and righteous action. This frames the focus’s حُسْنًا as morally accountable conduct.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:7\",\"ar\":\"لِنَبْلُوَهُمْ أَيُّهُمْ أَحْسَنُ عَمَلًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:104\",\"ar\":\"وَهُمْ يَحْسَبُونَ أَنَّهُمْ يُحْسِنُونَ صُنْعًا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:87\",\"ar\":\"أَمَّا مَن ظَلَمَ فَسَوْفَ نُعَذِّبُهُۥ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:88\",\"ar\":\"وَأَمَّا مَنْ ءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus presents goodness as a choice about how to treat a people; the following verses evaluate those alternatives by conduct and faith.\",\"limits\":\"أَحْسَنُ, يُحْسِنُونَ, and الْحُسْنَىٰ are distinct forms in different contexts. They establish a surah-wide evaluative frame, but do not set out the precise standard for the first encounter.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
